@title Drift Harbor client patch rollback runbook
@subtitle Owned by Live Ops. Version 2026-10-13
@author Quillfeather Interactive, Live Ops

## When to roll back
Roll back after a patch release when either condition holds:
- The crash rate is above 2% of sessions for 15 minutes.
- Login failures are above 5% for 10 minutes.

The Live Ops lead must approve the rollback in the #liveops-war-room channel.

## Do not roll back if
The patch contained a database schema migration, such as migration 0087 in patch 4.13. In that case, go forward with a hotfix instead, because older clients cannot read the new schema.

!!! Rolling back after a schema migration corrupts player inventories.

## Rollback steps
1. Stop the bleeding.
-- a) Pause the deploy pipeline.
-- b) Set matchmaking to maintenance mode with the in-game message "Back soon".
2. Point players to the last good build.
-- a) In the release console, set the live manifest to build 4.12.3.
-- b) Invalidate the CDN cache. This takes about 10 minutes.
3. Verify.
-- a) Install the build on 3 test accounts, one each on PC, console and mobile.
-- b) Confirm login and a full match on each.
4. Reopen in stages.
-- a) Let in 10% of players.
-- b) After 5 minutes, let in 25%.
-- c) After 5 more minutes, let in 50%.
-- d) After another 5 minutes, let in 100% if the crash rate stays under 1%.
5. Communicate.
-- a) Post a status update within 30 minutes of the decision.
-- b) Schedule compensation of 500 gems for every active account.

